{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018hVUzS1Kt2xGxMkaNwE1nf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\timport { NextResponse } from \"next/server\";\n2\timport type { NextRequest } from \"next/server\";\n3\timport { beds24Client } from \"@/lib/beds24-client\";\n4\timport type { ChannelManagerBooking } from \"@/lib/channel-manager-types\";\n5\t\n6\t// POST: Sync booking to channel manager\n7\texport async function POST(request: NextRequest) {\n8\t  try {\n9\t    const body = await request.json();\n10\t    const { checkIn, checkOut, roomType, guestName, guestEmail, guestPhone } = body;\n11\t\n12\t    if (!checkIn || !checkOut || !roomType || !guestName || !guestEmail || !guestPhone) {\n13\t      return NextResponse.json({ error: \"Missing fields\" }, { status: 400 });\n14\t    }\n15\t\n16\t    const checkin = new Date(checkIn);\n17\t    const checkout = new Date(checkOut);\n18\t    if (isNaN(checkin.getTime()) || isNaN(checkout.getTime()) || checkout <= checkin) {\n19\t      return NextResponse.json({ error: \"Invalid dates\" }, { status: 400 });\n20\t    }\n21\t\n22\t    const nights = Math.ceil(\n23\t      (checkout.getTime() - checkin.getTime()) / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24),\n24\t    );\n25\t\n26\t    const isPremium = roomType === \"Premium Capsule Pod\";\n27\t    const booking: Partial<ChannelManagerBooking> = {\n28\t      roomId: isPremium ? \"premium-capsule\" : \"standard-capsule\",\n29\t      guestName,\n30\t      guestEmail,\n31\t      guestPhone,\n32\t      checkin: checkin.toISOString().split(\"T\")[0],\n33\t      checkout: checkout.toISOString().split(\"T\")[0],\n34\t      nights,\n35\t      adults: body.adults || 1,\n36\t      totalPrice: (isPremium ? 45 : 35) * nights,\n37\t      currency: \"MYR\",\n38\t      status: \"confirmed\",\n39\t      source: \"website\",\n40\t      createdAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n41\t    };\n42\t\n43\t    const synced = await beds24Client.syncBooking(booking);\n44\t    return NextResponse.json({ success: true, synced });\n45\t  } catch (error) {\n46\t    console.error(\"Sync error:\", error);\n47\t    return NextResponse.json({ error: \"Failed\" }, { status: 500 });\n48\t  }\n49\t}\n50\t\n51\t// GET: Check availability\n52\texport async function GET(request: NextRequest) {\n53\t  const params = request.nextUrl.searchParams;\n54\t  if (params.get(\"action\") !== \"check\") {\n55\t    return NextResponse.json({ error: \"Invalid action\" }, { status: 400 });\n56\t  }\n57\t\n58\t  const checkin = params.get(\"checkin\");\n59\t  const checkout = params.get(\"checkout\");\n60\t  const roomId = params.get(\"roomId\");\n61\t\n62\t  if (!checkin || !checkout || !roomId) {\n63\t    return NextResponse.json({ error: \"Missing params\" }, { status: 400 });\n64\t  }\n65\t\n66\t  const availability = await beds24Client.getAvailability(checkin, checkout);\n67\t  const room = availability.find((a) => a.roomId === roomId);\n68\t\n69\t  if (!room) {\n70\t    return NextResponse.json({ available: false }, { status: 404 });\n71\t  }\n72\t\n73\t  return NextResponse.json({\n74\t    available: room.available > 0,\n75\t    availableUnits: room.available,\n76\t    totalUnits: room.total,\n77\t    rate: room.rate,\n78\t    currency: room.currency,\n79\t  });\n80\t}\n81\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"747c8b95-3597-4de2-850f-60587c80eb91","uuid":"d591c2bc-dff3-404d-af67-c66bb76e5a20","timestamp":"2026-04-14T01:54:09.013Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Jyue/Documents/1-projects/Software Projects/pelangi-website/site/src/app/api/bookings/sync/route.ts","content":"import { NextResponse } from \"next/server\";\nimport type { NextRequest } from \"next/server\";\nimport { beds24Client } from \"@/lib/beds24-client\";\nimport type { ChannelManagerBooking } from \"@/lib/channel-manager-types\";\n\n// POST: Sync booking to channel manager\nexport async function POST(request: NextRequest) {\n  try {\n    const body = await request.json();\n    const { checkIn, checkOut, roomType, guestName, guestEmail, guestPhone } = body;\n\n    if (!checkIn || !checkOut || !roomType || !guestName || !guestEmail || !guestPhone) {\n      return NextResponse.json({ error: \"Missing fields\" }, { status: 400 });\n    }\n\n    const checkin = new Date(checkIn);\n    const checkout = new Date(checkOut);\n    if (isNaN(checkin.getTime()) || isNaN(checkout.getTime()) || checkout <= checkin) {\n      return NextResponse.json({ error: \"Invalid dates\" }, { status: 400 });\n    }\n\n    const nights = Math.ceil(\n      (checkout.getTime() - checkin.getTime()) / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24),\n    );\n\n    const isPremium = roomType === \"Premium Capsule Pod\";\n    const booking: Partial<ChannelManagerBooking> = {\n      roomId: isPremium ? \"premium-capsule\" : \"standard-capsule\",\n      guestName,\n      guestEmail,\n      guestPhone,\n      checkin: checkin.toISOString().split(\"T\")[0],\n      checkout: checkout.toISOString().split(\"T\")[0],\n      nights,\n      adults: body.adults || 1,\n      totalPrice: (isPremium ? 45 : 35) * nights,\n      currency: \"MYR\",\n      status: \"confirmed\",\n      source: \"website\",\n      createdAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n    };\n\n    const synced = await beds24Client.syncBooking(booking);\n    return NextResponse.json({ success: true, synced });\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(\"Sync error:\", error);\n    return NextResponse.json({ error: \"Failed\" }, { status: 500 });\n  }\n}\n\n// GET: Check availability\nexport async function GET(request: NextRequest) {\n  const params = request.nextUrl.searchParams;\n  if (params.get(\"action\") !== \"check\") {\n    return NextResponse.json({ error: \"Invalid action\" }, { status: 400 });\n  }\n\n  const checkin = params.get(\"checkin\");\n  const checkout = params.get(\"checkout\");\n  const roomId = params.get(\"roomId\");\n\n  if (!checkin || !checkout || !roomId) {\n    return NextResponse.json({ error: \"Missing params\" }, { status: 400 });\n  }\n\n  const availability = await beds24Client.getAvailability(checkin, checkout);\n  const room = availability.find((a) => a.roomId === roomId);\n\n  if (!room) {\n    return NextResponse.json({ available: false }, { status: 404 });\n  }\n\n  return NextResponse.json({\n    available: room.available > 0,\n    availableUnits: room.available,\n    totalUnits: room.total,\n    rate: room.rate,\n    currency: room.currency,\n  });\n}\n","numLines":81,"startLine":1,"totalLines":81}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_015B7UjMNYN2Vqq2nrXb8bPV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see. These are Route Handlers (API routes), which don't support cacheSignal(). However, I can still implement the feature by:\n\n1. Creating a wrapper around the fetch in beds24-client.ts that uses cache() from React\n2. Since cache() works in Server Components, I need to create a Server Component or utility that wraps the fetch with cache() and cacheSignal()\n3. Or, I can modify the beds24Client methods to support cacheSignal() when called from Server Components\n\nActually, looking at the React docs and React 19.2, cacheSignal() can only be used within the cache() function scope. The pattern is:\n\n```typescript\nimport { cache, cacheSignal } from 'react';\n\nconst getCachedData = cache(async (url: string) => {\n  const res = await fetch(url, { signal: cacheSignal() });\n  return res.json();\n});\n```\n\nSo I need to:\n1. Import `cache` and `cacheSignal` from React\n2. Wrap the fetch call in the Beds24Client.getAvailability method with cache()\n\nHowever, this requires a bit of refactoring. Let me think about the best approach:\n\n**Option 1:** Create a new file `site/src/lib/cached-beds24-client.ts` that exports a cached version of the getAvailability function.\n\n**Option 2:** Modify the beds24-client.ts to add a cached variant.\n\nI think Option 1 is cleaner. Let me create a new file that wraps the fetch with cache() and cacheSignal().\n\nLet me check if there are any Server Components that fetch availability data (other than Route Handlers).","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2920,"cache_read_input_tokens":78252,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2920},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"747c8b95-3597-4de2-850f-60587c80eb91","uuid":"78f5fb26-7272-40f2-8b55-28fdd46cacc0"}
