{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_0197WPZa6U7TCK8XqcQmUkww","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No React imports in the lib. Let me now create my implementation plan.\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\n**Story US-162:** Add React 19.2 cacheSignal() for Server Component fetch cleanup\n\n### What needs to be done:\n1. Create a new file `site/src/lib/cached-availability.ts` that exports a cached version of getAvailability\n2. This file will:\n   - Import `cache` and `cacheSignal` from React\n   - Import the Beds24Client\n   - Export a `getCachedAvailability` function that wraps the fetch with cache() and cacheSignal()\n\n3. Update the Route Handlers to use the cached function (optional - just for demonstration)\n4. Verify TypeScript compilation passes\n5. Verify no regressions\n\n### Files to create:\n- `site/src/lib/cached-availability.ts` (new file)\n\n### Files to modify:\n- `site/src/app/api/ari/route.ts` (to use cached version)\n- `site/src/app/api/bookings/sync/route.ts` (to use cached version)\n\nWait, actually, I should think about this more carefully. The challenge with cacheSignal() is that it only works inside cache(). And the current beds24-client is a class with methods that do async work.\n\nThe cleanest approach would be to:\n1. Create a wrapper function that uses cache() and cacheSignal()\n2. Inside that, call the beds24Client.getAvailability method\n3. Export it for use in Server Components / Route Handlers\n\nActually, I realize now that Route Handlers are also Server Components (they run on the server). So cacheSignal() should work there too!\n\nLet me create the implementation:","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":780,"cache_read_input_tokens":83330,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":780},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"747c8b95-3597-4de2-850f-60587c80eb91","uuid":"3486c4c8-10f5-4c87-9f72-e84939c6d023"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_0197WPZa6U7TCK8XqcQmUkww","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Current State\n\nThe project uses React 19.2.0 and Next.js 16.1.6, which both support cacheSignal(). The beds24Client currently fetches availability data via HTTP requests but doesn't use React's cache() function or cacheSignal() for cleanup. Route Handlers at `/api/ari` and `/api/bookings/sync` call beds24Client.getAvailability().\n\n## Problem Identified\n\nThe acceptance criteria require:\n1. At least one cache() function wrapping an external fetch uses cacheSignal()\n2. Fetch requests are aborted when cache entry is invalidated\n3. No TypeScript errors with React 19.2 types\n4. Server Component rendering not regressed\n\nThe beds24-client.ts currently doesn't use React's cache() API, so in-flight fetch requests aren't automatically cleaned up when cached results are invalidated.\n\n## Planned Changes\n\n- Create new file `site/src/lib/cached-availability.ts` with:\n  - Import `cache` and `cacheSignal` from React\n  - Export `getCachedAvailability(checkin, checkout)` function that wraps the fetch call\n  - Use cacheSignal() to pass abort signal to fetch\n  - Call beds24Client internally\n\n- Update `site/src/app/api/ari/route.ts` to use the cached function\n- Run TypeScript check and build to verify no errors\n- Test that availability data still fetches correctly\n\n<plan>\n{\n  \"files_to_create\": [\"site/src/lib/cached-availability.ts\"],\n  \"files_to_modify\": [\"site/src/app/api/ari/route.ts\"],\n  \"functions_to_add\": [\"getCachedAvailability\"],\n  \"estimated_loc\": 80\n}\n</plan>\n\nNow let me implement the solution:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":780,"cache_read_input_tokens":83330,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":780},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"747c8b95-3597-4de2-850f-60587c80eb91","uuid":"56f5ce52-3ec6-4179-961e-b01910ea5f7d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_0197WPZa6U7TCK8XqcQmUkww","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NhYT9Q2LW4DhEuTE9GxfWP","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:/Users/Jyue/Documents/1-projects/Software Projects/pelangi-website/site/src/lib/cached-availability.ts","content":"import { cache, cacheSignal } from \"react\";\nimport { beds24Client } from \"./beds24-client\";\nimport type { ChannelManagerAvailability } from \"./channel-manager-types\";\n\n/**\n * Cached availability fetch with automatic cleanup via React's cacheSignal().\n *\n * In React 19.2, cache() + cacheSignal() allows in-flight fetch requests to be\n * aborted when the cache entry's lifetime ends. This prevents unnecessary network\n * connections from staying open when the cached result will no longer be used.\n *\n * cacheSignal() fires when:\n * - The cache entry is invalidated mid-request\n * - The Server Component completes rendering\n * - The cache duration expires\n *\n * Pattern: const signal = cacheSignal(); // Inside cache() scope\n *         const res = await fetch(url, { signal });\n */\nexport const getCachedAvailability = cache(\n  async (\n    checkin: string,\n    checkout: string,\n  ): Promise<ChannelManagerAvailability[]> => {\n    // Signal that fires when cache entry's lifetime ends, allowing fetch cleanup\n    const signal = cacheSignal();\n\n    // Get the base URL from config (same as beds24Client)\n    const baseUrl = \"https://api.beds24.com/api/v2.1\";\n    const apiKey = process.env.BEDS24_API_KEY || \"\";\n    const propertyId = process.env.BEDS24_PROPERTY_ID || \"\";\n\n    if (!apiKey || !propertyId) {\n      // Fall back to placeholder if not configured\n      return beds24Client.getAvailability(checkin, checkout);\n    }\n\n    try {\n      const params = new URLSearchParams({\n        apiKey,\n        propid: propertyId,\n        checkin,\n        checkout,\n      });\n\n      // Pass cacheSignal() as the abort signal so fetch is cleaned up\n      // when the cache entry is invalidated or lifetime expires\n      const response = await fetch(`${baseUrl}/getAvailability?${params}`, {\n        signal,\n        cache: \"no-store\",\n      });\n\n      if (!response.ok) {\n        console.error(\"Beds24 API error:\", response.statusText);\n        return beds24Client.getAvailability(checkin, checkout);\n      }\n\n      const data = await response.json();\n\n      // Parse the response using the same logic as beds24Client\n      if (!data || typeof data !== \"object\" || !(\"roomtypes\" in data)) {\n        return beds24Client.getAvailability(checkin, checkout);\n      }\n\n      const roomData = data as Record<string, unknown>;\n      const roomtypes = roomData.roomtypes;\n\n      if (!Array.isArray(roomtypes)) {\n        return beds24Client.getAvailability(checkin, checkout);\n      }\n\n      return roomtypes\n        .map((room: unknown) => {\n          if (typeof room !== \"object\" || !room) return null;\n          const r = room as Record<string, unknown>;\n\n          const roomId = String(r.id || r.roomId || \"\");\n          const roomName = String(r.name || r.roomName || \"\");\n          const available = Number(r.available || 0);\n          const total = Number(r.totalInventory || r.total || 0);\n          const rate = Number(r.rate || 0);\n\n          return {\n            roomId,\n            roomName,\n            checkin,\n            checkout,\n            available,\n            total,\n            rate,\n            currency: \"MYR\",\n          };\n        })\n        .filter((r): r is ChannelManagerAvailability => r !== null && r.roomId !== \"\");\n    } catch (error) {\n      console.error(\"Cached availability fetch failed:\", error);\n      return beds24Client.getAvailability(checkin, checkout);\n    }\n  },\n);\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":780,"cache_read_input_tokens":83330,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":780},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"747c8b95-3597-4de2-850f-60587c80eb91","uuid":"86518da0-eef1-4c28-afda-8b86ff049c57"}
